<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46795" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦκα</span></b> , Adv.: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> of Place or Motion, <i>slightly, a
			little</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦκ᾽ ἐπ᾽ ἀριστερά</span>
			<i>a little</i> to the left, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.336
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ. παρακλίνας κεφαλήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					20.301
				</span></i>
			: hence, generally, <i>softly, gently</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ. ἐλάσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					18.94
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				92
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπώσατο ἦ. γέροντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.508
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ. μάλα ψύξασα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					20.440
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ. κιόντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.254
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ. βιησάμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					226
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of Sound,
				<i>softly, low</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ. πρὸς ἀλλήλους ἀγόρευον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.155
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ. μύρεσθαι, μάλ᾽
			ὁμαδῆσαι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.463
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				565
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> of Sight,
				<i>softly, smoothly</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ.
				στίλβοντας ἐλαίῳ</span> with oil <i>soft</i>-shining,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.596
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦκ᾽ ἐπιμειδήσας</span>
			<i>soft</i>-smiling, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				547
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ. μέλαν</span>
			<i>slightly</i> black, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				3.39
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> of Time,
				<i>by little and little,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				5.278
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.), <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				2.67
			</span></i>. (Perh. connected with Lat. <i>sēg-nis</i> (for
				<i>sēg-nis</i>): but <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάκα</span> (i.e. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝᾶκα</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">:
			ἡδέως</span>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥσσων, ἥκιστος,
				ἤκιστος, ἠκαῖον, ἤκαλος, ἠκαλέον</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
